In JavaScript, you can use `console.time()` and `console.timeEnd()` to measure the execution time of a function. Here's a quick example:

```javascript
function myFunction() {
  console.time("myFunction");
  // Your code here
  console.timeEnd("myFunction");
}
```

This will print the time taken for the function to run, including the time it takes to execute the code inside it. You can also use `performance.now()` for more precise timing.

