I'd love to help! Here's a quick example of a three-column grid with a sticky sidebar:

```css
.container {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr;
  gap: 10px;
  margin: 10px;
}

.sidebar {
  width: 200px;
  height: 100vh;
  background: #f0f0f0;
  position: sticky;
  top: 0;
  z-index: 1;
}
```

This creates three equal columns and a sidebar that sticks to the top. You can adjust the `width` of the sidebar or the `grid-template-columns` as needed.

